What only Flatshare's make-room variant has, on #65282 and #65283: the switches from
--additional-config's make_room table, the reserve, the retention of realtime prefixes, and the log line of the PRs'
counters and its own.

The scheduler.py part of these commits on vLLM v0.33.0 (4ba787ec9):

  97f3ec3c7 Leaseholder make-room variant: switches, reserve and log line (cherry-picked from 5f96ab21c)
  1d108d69d Leaseholder make-room variant: keep realtime prefixes on the GPU between turns (cherry-picked from e176b99fa)
  d1c887685 Leaseholder make-room variant: count the retained blocks once (cherry-picked from 15b66b572)
  685080fcf Leaseholder make-room variant: recompute a realtime request's short load (cherry-picked from 7ce8f3588)
    Backported to v0.33.0: the rule follows 0.33.0's cap of the external hit
    for auxiliary outputs, so that it judges the load that is left.
  ef3e09e40 Leaseholder make-room variant: hold prefill from a call's announced turn (cherry-picked from 43e3f5a48)
  c024c2252 Leaseholder make-room variant: log the turns announced (cherry-picked from 27a501075)
  2fdfd47a1 Leaseholder make-room variant: keep the log line as it was without hints (cherry-picked from 95e8f4617)
  b2049e71a Leaseholder make-room variant: let a request take a lower priority's reservations (cherry-picked from 225b2e800)
  1ba908026 Leaseholder make-room variant: name the switch in the reservations' comment (cherry-picked from 9040a6895)
  0e89b549c Leaseholder make-room variant: hold lower-priority decodes from a request's first tokens (cherry-picked from 68e75d034)

